{
  "an10.172:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 10.172 ",
  "an10.172:0.2": "17. With Jānussoṇi ",
  "an10.172:0.3": "Bad Principles (2nd) ",
  "an10.172:1.1": "“Mendicants, you should know bad principles and good principles. ",
  "an10.172:1.2": "And you should know bad results and good results. ",
  "an10.172:1.3": "Knowing these things, your practice should follow the good principles with good results.” ",
  "an10.172:1.4": "That is what the Buddha said. ",
  "an10.172:1.5": "When he had spoken, the Holy One rose from his seat and entered his dwelling. ",
  "an10.172:2.1": "Soon after the Buddha left, those mendicants considered, ",
  "an10.172:2.2": "“The Buddha gave this brief summary recital, then entered his dwelling without explaining the meaning in detail. ",
  "an10.172:2.3": "‘You should know bad principles and good principles. ",
  "an10.172:2.4": "And you should know bad results and good results. ",
  "an10.172:2.5": "Knowing these things, your practice should follow the good principles with good results.’ ",
  "an10.172:2.6": "Who can explain in detail the meaning of this brief summary recital given by the Buddha?” ",
  "an10.172:3.1": "Then those mendicants thought, ",
  "an10.172:3.2": "“This Venerable Mahākaccāna is praised by the Buddha and esteemed by his sensible spiritual companions. ",
  "an10.172:3.3": "He is capable of explaining in detail the meaning of this brief summary recital given by the Buddha. ",
  "an10.172:3.4": "Let’s go to him, and ask him about this matter. ",
